WEBVTT

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:10.100
And so the unattractive young men run,

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.160
with nothing on their 
minds but obtaining

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.310
aphrodisiacs to win a girl's heart.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:18.470
Will they succeed in 
achieving their ambition?

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:23.750
Sorry, but tomorrow's out, 
and by the day after...

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.440
We'll be devouring those girls.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.170
A crisis for maidens!

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:36.010
The spring festival of earthly 
desires enters its third day...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.690
Moyashimon

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.260
<i>Good morning.</i>

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:01.520
<i>It's the third day of the spring 
festival, and the skies are clear.</i>

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.070
<i>Now for an important announcement 
from the agricultural society.</i>

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.060
What important announcement?

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:08.480
<i>For those students who are spending</i>

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.330
<i>the festival stuck in dirty clothes,</i>

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.900
<i>we are distributing free clothes</i>

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.780
<i>that were made here at the university.</i>

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.830
<i>Get them while they last!</i>

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.830
That's it?

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.200
Actually, I do kind of stink.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.830
Free Clothes
Earth-friendly

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.830
Bamboo 
Fiber

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.830
Free!!

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.830
T-shirts

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.830
Underwear

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:26.620
Youth

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.590
Talk about lame.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:29.890
Lame? This is just sad.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:32.200
Don't complain, just wear them.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.380
We live in an on-campus dorm. 
We have clothes.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.240
<i>This is the agricultural 
society's reserve corps</i>

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.620
<i>with a message to all students.</i>

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.510
News from the enemy?

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.060
<i>We hereby declare that, 
by the end of day three,</i>

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.290
<i>we will eliminate all surviving students</i>

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:46.770
<i>and conclude the spring festival.</i>

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.540
<i>If all students are eliminated,</i>

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.220
<i>they will be forced to do 
100 days of volunteer work.</i>

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.350
<i>That is all.</i>

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:54.840
Huh?

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.520
What?

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.770
So today's the big showdown.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.700
The Battle to Capture the Main Gate

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.720
Misato! Kawahama!

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:11.990
The rumor that you can get 100,000 
agris for defeating their boss

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.290
was apparently true.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.430
Seriously?

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.300
But it won't be easy to attack the gate.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.880
Don't worry.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.560
We're going to spread the 
word to all the survivors.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.760
All the survivors will attack 
the gate together at 4 PM.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:25.570
What?

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:26.760
Do we really have a chance?

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.900
The meteorology club did 
some simulations for us,

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.520
and determined that 4 PM will 
be the best time to attack.

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.010
What do you mean?

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.520
Why 4 PM?

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.970
According to the meteorology 
club's studies,

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:46.370
Building

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:46.370
Boss

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:46.370
Building

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.920
in front of the gate is mostly in 
the shade during the day,

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.130
but when the sunlight shines 
from the west in the evening,

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.370
the area in front of the 
boss is briefly in sunlight.

00:03:46.850 --> 00:03:51.000
They've found that 4 PM is when 
that area gets the most sun.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.720
In other words, since the enemy 
can only fight in shadows,

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.680
they'll have no choice but to 
fight at a distance from the boss.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:00.510
That's where we launch 
a full-scale attack.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.050
What do you think?

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.630
This is the single best strategy,

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:06.510
thought up by our 
student-run dorm resistance.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.260
I-I see.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.020
What's this "student-run 
dorm resistance," anyway?

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.390
Anyway, you guys think of a way

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:17.230
to defeat the boss yourselves 
using that strategy.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.530
We'll invite as many people as 
we can to join the offensive.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.290
We'll be counting on you

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:24.360
to arrange that party with 
the Itsuki seminar girls.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.780
Catch you later.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.200
So that's what motivates them...

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.400
But will that really work?

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:32.590
We'll make it work.

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.120
There's no turning back now.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.010
We'll meet in the lab to plan 
our strategy until then.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:37.640
Right.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:38.640
Yeah.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.220
'Sup!

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.560
Morning!

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.420
It's Team Hasegawa...

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:57.060
Wh-Why are you all dressed like that?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.190
Hasegawa-san was the only one who 
brought clothes to change into.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.680
I'm more impressed that you're 
wearing that shirt, Sawaki.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:07.010
I'd say it makes more sense 
than what you're wearing.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:11.740
Hey!

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:12.990
Don't try to run!

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.310
The agricultural society 
guys are at a disadvantage.

00:05:15.310 --> 00:05:16.690
H-Hey!

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.380
Those are the three guys who are 
after Professor Itsuki's aphrodisiacs!

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.370
They're really going at it.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.380
They're serious.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.730
You're mine!

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:30.750
Crap!

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:31.800
An ambush!

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.480
No fair making shadows yourselves!

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.730
How many of them are there?!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.230
Yer out!

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:47.150
Our rivals are out of 
the picture, but...

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.060
The agricultural society's tough.

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.620
We've gotta come up with a plan.

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.880
Hey... you think they 
overheard our strategy?

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:11.330
I bet the people who don't want 
the festival to end yet told them.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.930
Aren't Misato and his buddies here yet?

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.720
It's 4 PM!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.030
Hurry!

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.060
Those 100,000 agris are ours!

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.000
Push them back!

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.420
There are a lot of liberal 
arts people here, too!

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.320
Don't wuss out!

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:28.320
What's up, you pimply jerk?!

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.990
C.   diptheroid

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.990
I oughta brew your ass up!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:29.990
P.   acnes

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.170
You can do it, humans!

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:31.740
T.   tonsurans

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:33.950
Don't get stepped on, guys!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:33.970
M.   furfur

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.260
Don't lose!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.920
Reach the boss even if it 
takes us down to the last man!

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.650
Misato and his buddies 
still aren't here?!

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:45.420
Please, God! Get here soon!

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.600
What are they doing?!

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.350
Go take out Whiskers and Fatso!

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:58.640
Let's go, Kawahama!

00:06:58.640 --> 00:06:59.310
Right!

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.690
We're not gonna lose!

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:15.080
Kawahama! The rest is up to you!

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.820
There he is!

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.840
You're not getting past me!

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.550
<i>I have to get there!</i>

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.140
<i>I have to at least get there!</i>

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.350
<i>Here goes!</i>

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.900
<i>Go!</i>

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:53.660
What is that?

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.880
So... what am I supposed to do now?

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:07.930
Defeat him!

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.290
Our dreams are riding on you!

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:11.670
That doesn't really help me!

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.250
He's huge...

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:29.760
A-Are you serious?!

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.860
Is he a monster?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:34.840
All 
mixed 
together?!

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.780
No microbes here...

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:42.800
It's no good, Sawaki!

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:45.440
If you take a hit from 
him, you're done for!

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:49.340
I'm stuck!

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:53.800
Keep cool, Sawaki!

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.090
Just run away!

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.940
O-Okay!

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:58.820
That's it!

00:08:58.820 --> 00:08:59.600
Keep it up!

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:14.570
What's up with him?

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.470
Something's not right!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.740
Now that you mention it...

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:21.760
He has no skin microbes.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:26.030
What's wrong, Sawaki?

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:27.370
Leg cramp?

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.480
No...

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.240
<i>It couldn't be...</i>

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.550
Hey, what's the problem?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.330
The right leg isn't receiving 
the signal to advance!

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:45.270
What about the left leg?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:46.500
No good! We've got trouble!

00:09:46.500 --> 00:09:48.410
We have to reboot him!

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:49.790
Damn it!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.620
This is the biggest mistake the agricultural 
society cyber club could have made!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:56.400
Robo-Boss HQ

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:54.350
You there, time out!

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.400
Give us five minutes for maintenance!

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.590
You're mine!

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:19.490
Main Gate

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:23.740
I did it!

00:10:25.300 --> 00:10:26.660
All right!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:30.630
<i>This is an announcement from 
the agricultural society.</i>

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:34.030
<i>As of this moment, the spring 
festival is officially over.</i>

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:38.110
<i>Agricultural society members, 
please open all gates.</i>

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.660
<i>The running of outdoor stalls and use of</i>

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.120
<i>school tickets will continue until 8 PM.</i>

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:45.230
<i>You may now use cash, as well.</i>

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.370
Well, it's over.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:49.720
It was a little too fanatical 
for me this year, though.

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:52.530
We can finally walk around 
without these masks on!

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:54.320
Let's hit the stalls 
for drinks until 8 PM!

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.500
Hey, kid.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.170
Here's your 100,000 agris 
for defeating the boss.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:58.800
Take them.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:02.680
Sawaki!

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.210
You did it!

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:06.930
It really is 100,000...

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.190
Itsuki Keizou here. 
I believe you called me?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:18.270
Give us the aphrodisiacs!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.550
Excellent! Just as I'd 
expect of my students!

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:25.420
Let me know how they work for you!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.840
Yes! We finally got them!

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:30.650
Yeah!

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:31.710
Hey!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.710
You did it!

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:36.610
Huh?

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:44.720
Itsuki's Skin Whitening Set  
Try Me!

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:47.670
You think they'll fall for it?

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:49.140
It's worth a shot.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.940
It's better to see how they react

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:53.610
than to decide which one we each want.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:55.930
Then we just abandon 
ourselves to their choices,

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:57.220
and no hard feelings.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.400
Yes. Okay.

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.850
I'll be sure to tell Itsuki.

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:06.070
Goodbye.

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:18.150
These are Professor 
Itsuki's aphrodisiacs.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.670
Sh-She knew about them?!

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:23.930
You guys did this?

00:12:25.610 --> 00:12:27.220
D-Don't throw them away!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:29.930
Think of all we went 
through to get those!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:32.480
Aiming for Mutou and Oikawa?

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:35.190
W-Well, it's embarrassing to say,

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.940
but you're also one of the targets...

00:12:38.780 --> 00:12:40.440
Me? Whose target?

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.870
Here...

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.450
You're all idiots.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:50.450
Wow... so this is an aphrodisiac?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.770
Taste it, Hazuki-chan.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:53.960
No way!

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.190
You gotta be kidding!

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.220
So that's how you use that...

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.720
Well? Who am I supposed 
to fall in love with?

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:10.720
Me!

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:12.720
Get out of here!

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:17.350
Agricultural University Ramen Toppings

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:16.190
What the hell were these 
past three days, anyway?

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.860
Hey, shopkeeper! This ramen's too salty!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:25.200
Kawahama-san, your tears have 
been falling into the bowl.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.000
Care for some ramen? Half price!

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:28.000
Trade bowls with me, Sawaki.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.530
No freaking way.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:34.700
So, the spring festival is over.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.990
Professor, those 
aphrodisiacs didn't work.

00:13:37.990 --> 00:13:39.210
What? Really?

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:41.710
Anyway, I just got my 
hands on 100,000 yen

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:43.040
that someone threw away.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:45.220
Would you all care to go out 
for sukiyaki with me?

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.690
Yay!

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:49.720
I'll pass. I've got research to do.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.970
Then, Hasegawa-kun, 
could you do me a favor?

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:58.930
Hazuki-chan, have you heard what 
Hasegawa-san is like when she's drunk?

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:00.390
When she's drunk?

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.480
I thought she couldn't drink?

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.920
She can, but it's after she 
drinks that's the problem.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:08.700
Does she get mean?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.830
In a sense.

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.420
Oh, don't tell Sawaki-kun and 
the other guys about this.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:13.740
O-Okay...

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.970
I'm gonna drink tonight, Sawaki! 
Join me!

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.540
I'm underage...

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.520
Well, at least drink juice!

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:22.400
I'm in no mood to go back to the dorm!

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.720
Fine, but... you think 
Misato-san is okay?

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:26.260
Who cares?!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.780
Damn that Hasegawa!

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:34.860
What's up with him?

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:36.270
He's in a nasty mood.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.440
Making a damn fool of me!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.070
Hello there.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:48.030
This room looks as pathetic as always.

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:51.020
Wh-Wh-What are you doing here?

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:54.140
Professor Itsuki told me to bring these.

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:56.060
Probably to thank you for 
blowing 100,000

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:57.290
on aphrodisiacs that didn't work.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:15:00.790
And here's a list of the sake.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:03.300
Later.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.580
Hey, are these for real?

00:15:07.150 --> 00:15:10.300
Grad student... if these are real, 
they're incredible!

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:15.450
Isn't that bigger one the sake 
you had at Hiyoshi-san's bar?

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.060
His daiginjo sake was unprocessed,

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:20.520
Daiginjo is very high quality sake, and nakadori is said to be the highest quality

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:20.520
but this is from the 
unfiltered nakadori batch!

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.810
Nakadori?!

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.810
Yes! It's the finest of the fine!

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:27.820
What's the other bottle?

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.640
This one is awamori.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:34.320
This says it's pure vintage, 
aged for 200 years.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.830
200 years?! There's no way!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:41.530
It's said that the oldest 
vintage sake is 140 years old!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.580
So you think it's a lie?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.580
Yes! It has to be!

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:46.300
Well, who cares?

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.090
I'm gonna enjoy it anyway.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:50.590
Wait a minute... 
you're going to drink it?

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:52.140
Of course I am.

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.950
Why?! If that list is accurate,

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:59.270
you're holding the ultimate 
sake and an Okinawan treasure!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.160
Which is why I should drink it.

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:06.780
Just so you know,

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.880
I'm only drinking this because my duty

00:16:08.880 --> 00:16:11.320
as a researcher demands it.

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.060
I'm just going to taste it and leave.

00:16:13.060 --> 00:16:14.860
Fine. Let's just start with the sake.

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:19.560
What is this stuff?

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.250
It's incredible!

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:26.950
Amazing...

00:16:26.950 --> 00:16:30.000
Just it being "nakadori" 
changes the flavor this much?

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.690
Yeah...

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:35.510
What do you think?

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:40.880
It's good, but it's just 
normal violet liqueur.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:42.520
And this is just regular chocolate.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.340
Is that right?

00:16:44.930 --> 00:16:46.590
I guess aphrodisiacs were just something

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:49.030
like a dream to people in the old times.

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:52.780
Hasegawa-san tried all four, 
and she was totally fine.

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:55.660
But I wonder if she's really all right.

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:58.830
She drank all that liqueur in one gulp.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.290
That might be pushing her 
tolerance level to the edge.

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.490
I don't know about the vintage...

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:05.970
I'm sure it's good, but the flavor

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:08.360
of the last one will 
probably affect it...

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:12.920
What is it?

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.880
Do you like raw meat?

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:15.710
What?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:16.860
Raw meat.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:17.930
Uh... if it's yukhoe...

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.120
Can I bite off your ear?

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:22.760
Please don't.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.480
So what's your given name?

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.790
K-Kaoru.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:34.410
Aww, that's cute!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:35.750
But I look like an old guy.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:36.970
Yeah, I know.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:38.460
Do you like raw meat?

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:39.450
Uh...

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:41.500
Can I bite off your nose?

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:43.240
Sorry, but no...

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:54.460
Hey...

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:55.470
Hm?

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.470
Are you going home, Aoi-chan?

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.470
Why? Are you, Hazuki?

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.780
Want to hit one more place?

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:04.970
Sounds good.

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.980
The power of aphrodisiacs, eh?

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:11.420
It's the power of microbes that brings

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.480
harmony between people.

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:18.180
Hey, Misato!

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:20.490
Want to go out for breakfast...

00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:24.490
Why?

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:26.730
I don't know.

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:30.950
Just laugh at me for not being 
able to do anything all night.

00:18:30.950 --> 00:18:33.000
N-No, no, you did the right thing.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:36.280
That's just a bomb in the 
shape of a woman, anyway.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:59.010
Idiot

00:19:03.420 --> 00:19:04.490
Did I...

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:07.180
It's no use... I can't remember...

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.800
Oh, good...

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:13.330
Hasegawa-san just left without a word.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:17.100
The iron rule for overcoming 
panic is to make your enemy

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.860
even more confused than you are.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.330
Good job, Kawahama!

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:22.890
They're so stupid.

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:25.740
So that's what happens to 
Hasegawa when she's drunk.

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:27.900
We'll have to be careful from now on.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:28.860
Yeah.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.330
Wait...

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.750
Wait a minute...

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:42.610
How did this happen?!

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:47.350
<i>The number you have dialed is</i>

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:50.730
<i>out of the service area, 
or the phone is turned off.</i>

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.920
<i>I can't get in touch with Kei at all.</i>

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.260
Moyashimon

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:27.260
Episode 8

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:27.260
Microbe Theater 8!

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:27.260
Microbe Theater

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:31.620
Hi! We're grass bacilli.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:31.260
What Is Grass Bacillus?

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:36.190
What Is Grass Bacillus?

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.530
We live on dead trees and leaves.

00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:34.590
Just like our name suggests!

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:37.770
But the most famous 
one of our kind is...

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:37.230
The Most Famous One is Natto

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:41.250
The Most Famous One is Natto

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:39.770
Hey, I'm Bacillus natto.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.270
I'm known as natto bacteria.

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:44.780
Today I'll teach you how 
we can be raised at home.

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:47.150
Just call it "how to make natto"!

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:46.800
How to Make Natto at Home

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:50.280
1. Leave some natto behind.

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:49.500
When you eat natto, 
leave a little bit behind.

00:21:50.300 --> 00:21:52.810
2. Boil soybeans.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:52.300
Boil soybeans.

00:21:52.810 --> 00:21:56.770
3. Mix the boiled soybeans with the leftover natto.

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:54.590
Mix the boiled soybeans with the

00:21:54.590 --> 00:21:56.790
leftover natto while they're still hot.

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:59.900
Cover the mixture and let 
it age in a warm place.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:22:08.800
4. Let it age in a warm place.

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:02.960
We can't work if it's cold.

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:05.150
Warm spots next to the 
refrigerator, TV, or computer 
monitor work well!

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:05.400
We love warm places.

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:08.800
Natto!

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:11.800
How to Make Natto at Home

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.350
Then, let it sit overnight 
and it's done.

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:13.540
That's all?

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:14.680
Yep, that's all.

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:16.700
However!

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:24.730
Notice! This is only an explanation of how natto is made. 
If other bacteria enter the mixture, 
it will not result in natto - it will result in decay! 
Just store this information in the back of your mind as general trivia!

00:22:16.700 --> 00:22:19.050
This doesn't mean we recommend 
making natto at home.

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:20.510
If you attempt to do so,

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:22.650
please remember to do 
this at your own risk.

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:24.320
Please remember.

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:29.740
In Microbe Theater 
Episode 9,

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:29.740
We'll Do the Brewing.

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:36.030
Next Week: 
"Cling to That Soft Skin"

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.350
Hasegawa-kun, have you seen 
what this Surströmming can do?
